 markets requiring on-device and real-time AI, including smartwatches and fitness trackers, augmented and virtual reality (AR/VR) glasses, smart rings, digital health monitors, security systems and access control, livestock tracking, crop monitoring, and factory automation. It offers its products through internal direct sales force, and through a network of distributors and sales representatives. The company was formerly known as Cubiq Microchip, Inc. and changed its name to Ambiq Micro, Inc. in October 2012. The company was incorporated in 2010 and is based in Austin, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Fumihide  Esaka | CEO & Director | Age 62 | Compensation: $1.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 200 people. Revenue per employee of $363K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers. Stock-based compensation of $34K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Ambiq Micro, Inc. is a small-cap technology business with a $987M market cap on $73M of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at -178% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 44%.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Net dilution runs at 10.4% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 4.7% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Technology peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 61% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.1% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $22.1M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Technology ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (43% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Sector under pressure with a 19.3% decline over the past 6 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 241% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Head to Head Survey: Ambiq Micro (NYSE:AMBQ) vs. Qnity Electronics (NYSE:Q)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/16/head-to-head-survey-ambiq-micro-nyseambq-vs-qnity-electronics-nyseq.html","date":"2026-11-16","timestamp":1794829648.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.924,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Comparing Ambiq Micro (AMBQ) and Its Competitors","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/15/comparing-ambiq-micro-ambq-and-its-competitors.html","date":"2026-11-15","timestamp":1794781733.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.844,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Ambiq